<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Ulster Med J</journal-id><journal-title>The Ulster Medical Journal</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0041-6193</issn></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">4082356</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2447990</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">4082356</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Articles</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Surgical experience in necrotising enterocolitis: a report of nineteen cases</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Potts</surname><given-names>S R</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Garstin</surname><given-names>W I H</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>04</month><year>1985</year></pub-date><volume>54</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><abstract><p>The results of operative intervention in 19 neonates with necrotising enterocolitis are reported. There were four deaths (21%) in the series. Intestinal perforation was the indication for surgery in 10 cases (55%), three of which did not survive. Timing of operative intervention can be optimised only by close liaison between experienced physicians and surgeons in order to avoid intestinal perforation.</p></abstract></article-meta></front><body><supplementary-material content-type="scanned-pages"><graphic xlink:href="ulstermedj00090-0066.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="61" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="ulstermedj00090-0067.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="62" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="ulstermedj00090-0068.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="63" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="ulstermedj00090-0069.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="64" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/></supplementary-material></body></article>